    "index": 3,
    "hash": "v/2QGl4CRgtyJeAwfRD+jBrJT+A=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:37:23.082Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "## Verified against the template, not the docs\n\n**The academy has not been updated for this** \u2014 its project-structure pages still describe the older scaffold (eslint/prettier scripts, a `dependencies` block). The template source is authoritative.\n\n`packageJsonTemplate` emits **no `dependencies` key at all**. It writes exactly `peerDependencies` and `devDependencies`, both alphabetically sorted. That is what makes a Powerhouse package installable into a host that already supplies the runtime: the host (Connect, Switchboard, or a reactor) owns `document-model`, `@powerhousedao/reactor-browser` and friends, and the package must not drag a second copy in. It also explains `\"files\": [\"/dist\"]` and `\"sideEffects\": false` \u2014 the compiled output ships, the source trees do not.\n\nLinting and formatting are **oxlint and oxfmt**:\n\n```json\n\"lint\":         \"oxlint --type-aware --type-check\",\n\"lint:fix\":     \"oxlint --type-aware --type-check --fix\",\n\"format\":       \"oxfmt\",\n\"format:check\": \"oxfmt --check\"\n```\n\n`--type-aware --type-check` means the lint step performs TypeScript type checking too, which is why lint failures in a fresh project can look like `tsc` errors. `tsc`, `tsc:watch`, `vitest` (`test`, `test:watch`, `test:coverage`) and `check-circular-imports` (dpdm over `./index.ts`) round out the scripts, alongside thin `ph-cli` passthroughs: `generate`, `connect`, `build`, `reactor`, `service`, `vetra`.\n\nThe project-files builder writes `.oxlintrc.json` and `.oxfmtrc.json` at the project root \u2014 there is no `.eslintrc` or `.prettierrc` to find. It also emits **`reactor/index.ts`**, a headless entry point, so the package can be booted without a browser host.\n\nOne inconsistency worth flagging: the scaffold's `\"service\": \"ph-cli service\"` script points at a command that is *not* registered in `phCliCommands` or `phCliCommandNames`, so it is not dispatchable \u2014 the same gap that makes the Launch docs' `ph service setup` / `ph service restart` instructions stale.\n\n_Source: `packages/codegen/src/templates/boilerplate/package.json.ts` and `packages/codegen/src/file-builders/boilerplate/generated-project-files.ts`, Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-13T14:37:22.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:37:23.082Z"
    }
  },
